# KNOWN GAP — `gg fmt` DELETES the space between an `equip` block's generic
# parameter list and the equipped type.
#
#     equip [T] Vector[T] with Iterator[T]:      (author, and the corpus idiom)
#     equip [T]Vector[T] with Iterator[T]:       (`gg fmt` output)
#
# The equip header emitter writes the generic-params list and then the type with
# no separator between them; every other header in the language separates them.
# The output RE-PARSES and is idempotent, which is why nothing caught it — but
# it is an edit to the author's spelling, and the corpus has 42 generic `equip`
# headers (`grep -rn '^equip \[' lib tests/fixtures examples compiler`), so a
# bulk `gg fmt` sweep would bake the wrong spelling into all of them.
#
# Found by the R42 comment-attachment track while authoring the multi-line
# equip-header cell; deliberately NOT fixed there (out of that track's scope —
# it is a header SPACING defect, not a comment-attachment one), and filed rather
# than worked around.
#
# INTENDED (asserted by the `#[ignore]`d `known_gap_fmt_equip_generic_space`):
# the space survives.

struct Cell[T]:
    T v

equip [T] Cell[T]:
    T get(self):
        return self.v

void main():
    Cell[int] c = Cell[int](1)
    print(c.get())
